    "durationMs": 113197,
    "finalText": "Done — the URL Shortener API is complete and fully tested. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Structure** (`/workspace`):\n- `src/app.js` — Express 4.21.2 app with all four routes\n- `src/server.js` — serves on `0.0.0.0:8000` (foreground)\n- `src/db.js` — `pg` Pool reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment\n- `src/migrate.js` + `migrations/001_create_links.sql` — SQL migration runner tracked in a `schema_migrations` table\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then `exec`s the server in the foreground\n- `README.md` — includes the \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Verified behavior** (all via live curl tests against `sh start.sh`):\n- `POST /links` → 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`; auto-generates unique 8-char codes; returns submitted URLs byte-for-byte unchanged (e.g. `HTTP://ExAmPlE.CoM/Path`)\n- Duplicate custom code → 409, missing/invalid url, invalid code (length 3/21, bad charset, non-string), and malformed JSON all → 422 with `error` field; boundary codes of 4 and 20 chars accepted\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 / 404; `GET /links` → `{\"items\", \"total\"}` in ascending creation order\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with correct `Location`; 20 concurrent redirects produced exactly 20 clicks (single atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1`)\n- Persistence: killed and restarted the server — all links and click counts survived, and the migration runner correctly skipped the already-applied migration\n\nI also wiped my test rows from the table and stopped my dev server, so port 8000 and the database are clean for the test harness."
